$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\- 8 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=-x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=-x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}4(x+(-x))^{2}-2(-x)-(2)&=0\\\\2x-(2)&=0\\\\2x&=2\\\\x&=1\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding point is $(1,-1)$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186521758 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521747 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186521758 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521755 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186521758 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521789 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186521758 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521839 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186521758 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521850 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186521758 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521860 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186521758 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186521758 #edb/ref 1071 "At which points on the curve $8 x y + 2 y^{2}=16 x^{2} + 432$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-3,-12)$\n- **II.** $(0,12)$\n- **III.** $(\\frac{3}{2},12)$\n- **IV.** $(3,0)$\n- **V.** $(3,6)$\n- **VI.** $(3,12)$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186521758 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "10aa9a22-24d9-5578-9f7c-cc0b57f6bc72" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186521758 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}8 x y + 2 y^{2}&=16 x^{2} + 432\\\\- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 2 y^{2} - 432)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 4 y)\\,i-(- 32 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangen